NAME
     readelf - look inside an ELF file

SYNOPSIS
     readelf [-h] [-l] [-d] [-s] [-r] [-a] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     readelf prints the parts of an ELF file that the options ask for.

OPTIONS
     -h   the header
     -l   the program headers (the segments)
     -d   the dynamic section
     -s   the symbol tables
     -r   the relocations
     -a   all of it

SEE ALSO
     nm(1), ldd(1), file(1)
